```java
@SpringBootTest
@Import(TestClockConfig.class)
class ConcurrencyTest {
    @Autowired TicketService tickets; @Autowired DisputeService disputes; @Autowired SettlementService settlements;
    @Autowired JdbcTemplate jdbc; @Autowired MutableClock clock;

    @BeforeEach cleanup same as base.

    long grossedTicket(String p) {
        long id = tickets.createTicket(new CreateTicketRequest(p+"-c","TO-SYN-0001","SYN-TRUCK-01")).body().id();
        tickets.recordTare(id, new TareRequest(p+"-t", 8000, T0));
        clock.set(GROSS);
        tickets.recordGross(id, new GrossRequest(p+"-g", 12000, GROSS));
        return id;
    }
```

concurrentAdjudication: submit reweigh (clock at GROSS+5). disputeId from jdbc. Two callables adjudicate with different requestIds, one REWEIGH one ORIGINAL. Run with latch. Collect outcomes: Result record (ok boolean, exception). Assert one ok one BizException 409. Then freeze with expectedReweighIds=[rwId] → ok; assert single dispute RESOLVED, single freeze; net consistent with adopted source.

concurrentFreeze: two threads freeze different requestIds → one ok, one 409; count=1.

reweighVsFreeze: thread A submitReweigh (clock GROSS+5), thread B freeze(expected []). Exactly one succeeds. Verify DB consistency.

Helper to run two callables concurrently:

```java
